<section id="progress" aria-labelledby="h-progress">
  <h2 id="h-progress" class="sec">Progress</h2>
  <p class="sub">Every closed-loop run that set a new best on its split, and whether the gain over the previous best clears the noise bar. Open-loop and pipeline-test runs are excluded. Runs on an explicit task list (split "custom") are listed but never compared, because the CSV does not record which tasks they used.</p>
  <div class="scroll"><table id="records"></table></div>
  <div class="charts" style="margin-top:12px">
    <div class="card chart" id="c-bars">
      <h2>Per-family score vs Genie 3</h2>
      <div class="chips" id="bar-chips" role="group" aria-label="Experiments to chart (up to 4)"></div>
      <div class="legend" id="bar-legend"></div>
      <div id="bar-svg"></div>
      <details><summary>Table view</summary><div id="bar-table"></div></details>
      <div class="tip" id="bar-tip" role="status"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card chart" id="c-line">
      <h2>Overall score over time</h2>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-bottom:4px;font-size:13px">Times are UTC. Hollow markers are open-loop (dataset) runs.</p>
      <div class="legend" id="line-legend"></div>
      <div id="line-svg"></div>
      <details><summary>Table view</summary><div id="line-table"></div></details>
      <div class="tip" id="line-tip" role="status"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="callout">Charts follow the leaderboard filters. In the grouped bar chart, bars start at 0 even though scores cannot go below 1.</p>
</section>
